[:db/add "1eb042b7-4390-5cc3-b683-bdc64a6141fc" :question/id #uuid "1eb042b7-4390-5cc3-b683-bdc64a6141fc"] [:db/add "1eb042b7-4390-5cc3-b683-bdc64a6141fc" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{5 y}{x},\\qquad x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 8 x^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- 16 x.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation."] [:db/add "1eb042b7-4390-5cc3-b683-bdc64a6141fc" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=- 8 x^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 8 x^{2}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-8\\cdot 2 x \\\\ &=- 16 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=- 8 x^{2}$ and $y\\prime=- 16 x$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5 y}{x} \\\\ - 16 x &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5\\left(- 8 x^{2}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 16 x &\\not\\equiv - 40 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 8 x^{2}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""] [:db/add "1eb042b7-4390-5cc3-b683-bdc64a6141fc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "1eb042b7-4390-5cc3-b683-bdc64a6141fc" :question/answer-fields "71481ca8-e7c8-5dea-9ec6-cf7e74d010d1"] [:db/add "1eb042b7-4390-5cc3-b683-bdc64a6141fc" :question/answer-fields "b240868a-780d-52d0-9567-8e15eefe7db1"] [:db/add "1eb042b7-4390-5cc3-b683-bdc64a6141fc" :question/answe