I is false. Substituting $y=- 5 x^{2}$ and $y\\prime=- 10 x$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3 y}{x} \\\\ - 10 x &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3\\left(- 5 x^{2}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 10 x &\\not\\equiv - 15 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 5 x^{2}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""] [:db/add "5fd7470a-4c69-539d-97c1-b0bef4d6487e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "5fd7470a-4c69-539d-97c1-b0bef4d6487e" :question/answer-fields "b2bea227-c17b-57ad-af47-5aaca6599235"] [:db/add "5fd7470a-4c69-539d-97c1-b0bef4d6487e" :question/answer-fields "486a0603-6f7f-522b-b3d6-01b52b4dddc7"] [:db/add "5fd7470a-4c69-539d-97c1-b0bef4d6487e" :question/answer-fields "e98f4f9d-447e-58a2-86b5-8024aca227a8"] [:db/ensure "5fd7470a-4c69-539d-97c1-b0bef4d6487e" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/questions "5fd7470a-4c69-539d-97c1-b0bef4d6487e"] [:db/ensure 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/validate]]
